    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "As one of our efforts in subsurface fracture network characterization this work shows how accurate we can predict a subsurface fracture system using limited wellbore data. Taking advantage of a huge natural fracture exposure (400m x 300m) in Colorado, USA we compare the joint system shown on the exposure with those predicted from a number of pseudo wells (4, 8, 14, and 60). The sensitivity of prediction to well number, fracture orientation, horizontal well, and different densities is also discussed. Our goals are to provide some guidance for improving the way we currently use to predict subsurface fracture system, and to provide some relationships between what we can see in wellbores and subsurface fracture system.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
